A pool destroy forgets the armed timers it takes.
The stall in wfi would wait for a timer that is gone;
the count of armed sources is exactly the armed timers and device Irqs.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: the count of armed sources is wrong

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -236,6 +236,2 @@
     }
-    case CAP_TIMER:
-        /* The timer is gone and will not fire, so it is no source. */
-        timer_set_bits((struct timer *)o, 0);
-        break;
     case CAP_IRQ: {
